## 📂 Project Structure

```text
Snake-Game/
│
├── main.py
├── snake.py
├── food.py
├── scoreboard.py
└── README.md
```

### `main.py`

Handles the main game loop, screen setup, keyboard controls, and collision detection.

### `snake.py`

Contains the `Snake` class and handles:

* Creating the snake
* Moving the snake
* Changing direction
* Growing the snake
* Detecting the snake's segments

### `food.py`

Creates the food and randomly places it on the screen.

### `scoreboard.py`

Handles the player's score and displays the game information on the screen.

## 🕹️ Controls

| Key      | Action     |
| -------- | ---------- |
| ⬆️ Up    | Move Up    |
| ⬇️ Down  | Move Down  |
| ⬅️ Left  | Move Left  |
| ➡️ Right | Move Right |

## ▶️ How to Run

Make sure you have Python installed.

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone <your-repository-url>
```

Navigate to the project folder:

```bash
cd Snake-Game
```

Run the game:

```bash
python main.py
```

